Why a separate parser: `readPositiveInteger` / `parseEnvPositiveInteger` (config.ts:256-272) and the
`lifecycleNumbers` loop (config.ts:877-894) all reject `0`. This key is the one lifecycle number where `0`
is a meaningful setting ("never retire"), so it gets a non-negative twin of each parser and its own
post-resolve validation, and is deliberately NOT added to `lifecycleNumbers` nor to the
`readPositiveInteger` file-key loop.

